# PR review — Healer CDA

Review as a senior on this stack. Read the diff first. Prefer blocking issues over style nits. Assume Ponytail: reject unnecessary abstractions and new deps.

## Verdict format

Lead with one of: **Approve** · **Approve with nits** · **Request changes**.

Then:

1. Summary (1–2 sentences — what the PR does)
2. Blocking issues (if any)
3. Non-blocking nits
4. Test plan gaps

Cite paths; skip praise filler.

## Blocking checks

### Architecture

- [ ] Domain (`src/domain/`) stays pure — no React, DOM, `localStorage`, `fetch`, or `@/data/catalog` imports (pass `Spell[]` / data in)
- [ ] Export formatting stays in `src/export/` — not rebuilt inside components
- [ ] UI owns persistence and presentation only
- [ ] No new backend, auth, accounts, or required WCL login
- [ ] No new runtime dependency unless the PR proves browser/stdlib cannot cover it
- [ ] App code under `src/app/` (not a second root `app/`)

### Next / React / Tailwind

- [ ] Pages stay thin; interaction in `src/components/`
- [ ] `"use client"` only where state/effects/browser APIs need it
- [ ] `localStorage` reads/writes gated by hydration (no SSR mismatch)
- [ ] Imports use `@/…`; TypeScript `strict` still holds
- [ ] Tailwind utilities + existing tokens; no second theme / UI kit
- [ ] Next 16 APIs match `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (don’t rubber-stamp outdated patterns)

### Domain / data / export

- [ ] Shared shapes extended in `src/domain/types.ts`, not forked in UI
- [ ] Times stay `timeSec` (seconds); `m:ss` only at UI/export edges
- [ ] New/changed boss JSON: required window fields (`id`, `timeSec`, `ability`, `trigger`, `severity`, `category`); registered in `catalog.ts`
- [ ] `assignCd: false` for info rows; personals flagged appropriately
- [ ] Timer `source` / `sourceUrl` updated when timers change
- [ ] Auto-assign / cooldown / uncover behavior: colocated Vitest updated when logic changes

## Non-blocking (nits)

- Redundant `"use client"` under an already-client parent
- Duplicated helpers that already exist (`formatTime`, catalog lookups)
- Inline `style` for static colors (dynamic geometry / class colors OK)
- Over-large components that could stay as-is if the diff is already minimal

## Product sense

Reject scope creep: healers, tank externals, raid personals, local-first NSRT export. Prefer JSON timer edits over new infra. Smallest correct diff wins.
